      {
        "kind": "text",
        "text": "The recent five quarterly increases average 25.2372 billion, supporting a higher drift than the full reference class. BEA's current methodology describes business R&D advance estimates as judgmental trends; corporate financial statements and Census quarterly services receipts enter later estimates. This favors trend continuation while leaving meaningful first-print uncertainty. No separate one-off or policy adjustment is supported by fetched evidence. Source: https://apps.bea.gov/scb/issues/2026/09-september/0926-nipa-methodologies.htm."
