      {
        "kind": "math",
        "text": "Prior/update/interval: Use a persistence-with-drift model fitted to 2023-Q1 through 2026-Q2. Level = 950.518; base drift = 15.226; momentum adjustment = 0.75*(25.2372-15.226) = 7.5084; discretionary one-off and policy adjustments = 0. Thus point = 950.518+15.226+7.5084 = 973.2524. Successive changes are [10.825,6.710,11.950,18.024,5.298,13.970,2.747,2.228,23.206,25.803,26.170,27.588,23.419]. Their squared deviations sum to 1050.53696, so sigma = 9.356535 = sqrt(1050.53696/12). The normal 80% half-width is 1.28*sigma = 11.976365. Multiply by a judgmental 1.5 to account for advance-estimation uncertainty that smooth revised history can understate: final half-width = 17.964547. Bounds = 955.287853 and 991.216947; rounded forecast = 973.25 with interval [955.29,991.22]. This interval is model-based, not calibrated against recovered original-vintage forecast errors."
